    "Write in the language you think in": "用你思考的语言写作",
    "By the Notara team · 5 min read": "Notara 团队 · 阅读约 5 分钟",
    "Most of us switch languages all day without noticing. We read documentation in one, chat with colleagues in another, and take notes in whatever comes first. The tools we use rarely make that easy.": "我们大多数人整天都在不知不觉地切换语言：用一种语言读文档，用另一种和同事聊天，记笔记时哪种先冒出来就用哪种。而我们用的工具很少让这件事变得轻松。",
    "When we started Notara, we wanted an editor that gets out of the way. That meant fewer buttons, quieter colors and an interface that feels familiar on the first day.": "开始做 Notara 时，我们想要一个不碍事的编辑器：更少的按钮、更安静的颜色，以及第一天就让人觉得熟悉的界面。",
    "Small words carry the most weight": "越短的词，分量越重",
    "A settings page is full of short labels: Small, Medium, Large. Out of context they are easy to translate and easy to get wrong, because the same word can answer very different questions.": "设置页里满是短标签：Small、Medium、Large。脱离上下文，它们很容易翻译，也很容易译错，因为同一个词可能在回答完全不同的问题。",
    "Good localization keeps the question next to the answer. It treats a group of options as one unit, so each choice reads naturally in the target language.": "好的本地化会让答案始终挨着问题：把一组选项当作一个整体，让每个选项在目标语言里都读起来自然。",
    "Keep what is yours": "属于你的，保持原样",
    "Your notes, names and titles belong to you. A translation layer should change the interface around them and leave your own words exactly as you wrote them.": "你的笔记、名字和标题属于你。翻译层应该改变它们周围的界面，而让你自己写下的文字保持原样。"
  }
